  "spec_section": "protocol.md §9.13 + §3.4 + §5.2 + §6.4",
  "description": "Pins protocol::encode_dictionary_blob_raw + protocol::decode_dictionary_blob byte mapping for the MYD1 vault.dictionary encrypted personal-dictionary codec (MYND-266; §9.13). The inner plaintext is OPAQUE (the desktop layer's serialized {personal_words, ignore_words} word sets) — no canonical-JSON discipline, unlike vault-prefs; the structural twin of vault.search/vault.workspace/vault.indices. personal_dictionary_key = derive_subkey(root_key, SubkeyRole::PersonalDictKey) (HKDF role 'personal-dictionary-key'); account_number_hash binds via aad_personal_dictionary_blob (AAD role 'personal-dictionary-blob' — a DISTINCT load-bearing string from the HKDF role). 12 cases: 3 encrypt (empty / small descriptor / 1-KB) + 1 decrypt_ok + 2 decrypt_aead_fail (tag-tamper + cross-vault, both non-distinguishing per §6.4, real-key fixtures) + 6 parse_fail (one per distinguishable pre-decryption structural reject incl. the load-bearing format_unsupported forward hook, §9.13.4). Cases generated by `cargo test -p protocol --lib emit_vault_dictionary_vectors_for_paste -- --ignored` (in protocol/src/dictionary_blob.rs).",
